title: April 2026

@rozwoj_association_2026
# prose-audit: Grade B — Morawiecki's named internal network is distinguished from a party or club, Lewica's position changes inside a PiS cabinet, and each response has an authored consequence; this remains the opening stage of a longer rupture.
title: Morawiecki builds the Rozwój+ association
subtitle: The former prime minister gives his PiS current a name, offices and a programme—but no independent seats
face-image: img/poland/events/mateusz-morawiecki-2023.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 23
order: 11
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and ((year = 2026 and month = 4) or (year = 2026 and month = 1 and rozwoj_early_route)) and rozwoj_association_active = 0 and pis_seats >= 5
on-arrival: {!
Q.rozwoj_association_active = 1;
Q.rozwoj_departure_pressure +=
    Math.max(
        0,
        50 - (Number(Q.united_right_cohesion) || 0)
    ) * 0.40 +
    Math.max(
        0,
        (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) - 35
    ) * 0.35;
Q.rozwoj_association_members = Math.min(
    34,
    Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.pis_seats) || 0))
);
Q.rozwoj_chain_stage = 1;
const association = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "rozwoj_plus";
});
const oldMorawieckiCaucus = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "morawiecki";
});
if (oldMorawieckiCaucus) {
    oldMorawieckiCaucus.active = 0;
    oldMorawieckiCaucus.mp_count = 0;
    oldMorawieckiCaucus.sejm_mps = 0;
    oldMorawieckiCaucus.legal_status = "absorbed into Rozwój+";
}
if (association) {
    association.active = 1;
    association.legal_status = "political association inside PiS";
    association.organisation = 38;
    association.cohesion = 54;
    association.mp_count = Q.rozwoj_association_members;
    association.sejm_mps = Q.rozwoj_association_members;
    association.senators = 0;
    association.meps = 3;
    association.defection_readiness = 24;
}
const associationPeople = [
    "morawiecki", "semieniuk", "cieszynski", "jablonski", "kwiecien",
    "bartosik", "lorek", "dworczyk", "muller"
];
for (const person of (Q.rival_person_records || [])) {
    if (associationPeople.includes(person.id)) {
        person.organisation = "rozwoj_plus";
        person.loyalty = "dual PiS and Rozwój+ loyalty";
        person.status = person.chamber == "Sejm"
            ? "PiS MP in Rozwój+ association"
            : "PiS MEP in Rozwój+ association";
    }
}
Q.news_headline = "Rozwój+ turns Morawiecki's network into an association";
!}

= April 2026 — Association before ultimatum

Former prime minister <span class="party-pis"><b>Mateusz Morawiecki</b></span>, still a PiS politician, opens the
first Rozwój+ convention under banners promising investment, technology and a
less punitive conservatism. PiS parliamentarians and former ministers
<span class="party-pis"><b>Olga Semeniuk-Patkowska</b></span>, <span class="party-pis"><b>Janusz Cieszyński</b></span> and <span class="party-pis"><b>Paweł Jabłoński</b></span> appear
on its organising lists. They retain their PiS membership and mandates.

Rozwój+ now has members, local activity and an internal programme. It is **not
a Sejm club and not a political party**. <span class="party-pis"><b>Jarosław Kaczyński</b></span>, PiS chair,
tolerates a current that still asks his permission to remain inside the
caucus; Morawiecki is building the ability to survive the day that permission
ends.

[? if government_party = "pis" and left_in_government: Lewica sits in a
PiS-led cabinet while its senior partner divides. A dialogue can stabilise the
government, an attack can hurry the rupture, and a policy concession can make
Morawiecki stronger without moving a single seat.?][? if government_party !=
"pis" or not left_in_government: For Lewica this is a rival organisation inside
a rival party. It may keep both PiS camps talking, test the new brand against
Morawiecki's record or give his current an issue victory inside PiS.?]

- @rozwoj_association_alliance
- @rozwoj_association_attack
- @rozwoj_association_social

@rozwoj_association_alliance
title: Offer a transparent economic-policy dialogue to both PiS camps
subtitle: Talk to Morawiecki without recognising a party that does not yet exist or letting Kaczyński claim exclusion.
on-arrival: rozwoj_party_readiness += 3; pis_relation += 2; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "Lewica opens a policy channel without recognising a new party"

Lewica invites Kaczyński's economic team and Morawiecki's association to the
same public roundtable on investment and industrial policy. Rozwój+ gains the
visibility of a separate voice, but the minutes still identify every one of
its deputies as PiS. Both camps keep our telephone number; neither receives
recognition of a split that has not happened.

- @poland_event_queue: Convene the roundtable

@rozwoj_association_attack
title: Attack Morawiecki's governing record and new developmental brand
subtitle: Put the Polish Deal, public services and labour enforcement beside the association's new promises.
on-arrival: rozwoj_departure_pressure += 5; rozwoj_party_readiness += 4; pis_relation -= 3; labor_credibility += 3; news_headline = "Lewica tests Rozwój+ against Morawiecki's record"

At the first press conference, Lewica answers the new logo with Morawiecki's
years as prime minister: the Polish Deal's disruption, centralised investment
and promises made without organised labour. Rozwój+ is forced to defend a
record it hoped to inherit selectively. The attack hardens its separate
identity even as it denies the rebrand a clean beginning.

- @poland_event_queue: Hold the press conference

@rozwoj_association_social
title: Offer an investment-and-worker-rights concession across the aisle
subtitle: Give Morawiecki an issue victory inside PiS and accept the argument this opens within Lewica.
on-arrival: rozwoj_departure_pressure -= 3; rozwoj_party_readiness -= 2; government_favors += 1; labor_credibility += 2; progressives_dissent += 2; news_headline = "A policy concession gives the developmental camp an inside-PiS win"

Lewica offers a joint package coupling regional investment to collective
bargaining and labour inspection. Morawiecki claims that Rozwój+ changed policy
without leaving PiS, exactly the proof he needs to postpone a rupture. Workers
gain an advocate across the aisle; our progressive wing asks why a former PiS
prime minister was allowed to present a Left condition as his achievement.

- @poland_event_queue: Table the joint package

@ko_leadership_2026
# prose-audit: Grade B — Tusk remains the formal leader while Nowacka, Sikorski and Kierwiński are introduced as real channels; four authored results replace stat-led exits, though the event maps influence rather than deciding a succession.
title: KO distributes influence after its 2025 convention
subtitle: Tusk keeps the chair while progressive, Atlanticist and organisational currents compete to become Lewica's doorway
face-image: img/poland/events/donald-tusk-2023.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 24
order: 10
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2026 and month = 4 and ko_collapsed = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.us_congress_channel =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.us_congress_channel))
        ? Number(Q.us_congress_channel)
        : 48;
Q.left_atlanticist_dissent =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.left_atlanticist_dissent))
        ? Number(Q.left_atlanticist_dissent)
        : 12;
Q.news_headline = Q.ko_consolidated
    ? "KO's consolidated party gives its internal currents national offices"
    : "KO's surviving organisations bargain over common national offices";
!}

= April 2026 — Channels, not a Left-appointed successor

<span class="party-ko"><b>[+ ko_leader +]</b></span> holds KO's national leadership. The question is not a
vacancy Lewica may fill; it is a division of access beneath the leader.[? if ko_consolidated:
 The consolidated KO party assigns national offices among networks that once
belonged to separate component organisations.?][? if not ko_consolidated: PO,
KO and the surviving component organisations bargain over common offices while
retaining their legal identities.?]

<span class="party-ko"><b>Barbara Nowacka</b></span>, KO's education-policy progressive, offers cooperation on
rights and public services. <span class="party-ko"><b>Radosław Sikorski</b></span>, its Atlanticist foreign-policy
voice, offers Washington and European security channels. <span class="party-ko"><b>Marcin Kierwiński</b></span>,
the party organiser, offers lists, county structures and quiet coalition
management. **[+ ko_leader +]** offers one accountable principal and no
insurance against what happens after them. [? if ko_leader != "Donald Tusk":
Whoever holds the chair now holds it because KO's 2025 convention decided it
could not keep the leader it had, which is exactly why the currents below are
still competing.?]

Lewica must choose which relationship it wants to deepen. The choice shifts
trust and influence inside KO; it does not appoint its leader or turn a contact
into a coalition agreement.

- @ko_nowacka
- @ko_sikorski
- @ko_kierwinski
- @ko_tusk

@ko_nowacka
title: Deepen the channel to Nowacka's progressive current
view-if: ko_leader != "Barbara Nowacka"
subtitle: Work together on schools, equality and services, while PSL sees another urban-progressive axis forming.
on-arrival: ko_channel_target = "Nowacka progressive channel"; ko_social_liberal_share += 5; ko_classical_liberal_share -= 5; progressive_credibility += 2; ko_relation += 3; psl_relation -= 2; news_headline = "Lewica deepens its channel to KO progressives"

Nowacka and Lewica's social-policy team announce joint parliamentary work on
schools, equality and public services. Her current gains weight inside KO
because it can produce cooperation beyond the party. PSL hears a metropolitan
progressive bloc taking shape and becomes less willing to settle social policy
in the same room.

- @poland_event_queue: Announce the joint work

@ko_sikorski
title: Build an Atlanticist coalition channel around Sikorski
view-if: ko_leader != "Radosław Sikorski"
subtitle: Join Sikorski on NATO and Washington, accepting that security will crowd the social agenda.
on-arrival: ko_channel_target = "Sikorski Atlanticist channel"; ko_relation += 5; us_congress_channel += 3; military_trust += 2; left_atlanticist_dissent -= 2; labor_dissent += 1; news_headline = "Security politics opens an Atlanticist coalition channel"

Sikorski brings Lewica representatives into regular briefings with Atlanticist
MPs and congressional contacts. The military no longer hears two incompatible
opposition or coalition messages from the democratic parties. Labour organisers
notice that the new common language has detailed answers for alliances and
another promise to return to wages later.

- @poland_event_queue: Join the briefings

@ko_kierwinski
title: Work through Kierwiński's organisational apparatus
view-if: ko_leader != "Marcin Kierwiński"
subtitle: Exchange constituency intelligence and coalition discipline away from the cameras.
on-arrival: ko_channel_target = "Kierwiński organisational channel"; ko_relation += 6; local_network += 2; barons_dissent -= 2; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "The coalition's organisational secretaries build a quiet compact"

Kierwiński's organisers and Lewica's regional secretaries begin comparing
committee votes, local conflicts and seats neither wants to gift to the right.
The arrangement solves problems before leaders need to dramatise them. When it
becomes visible, it looks exactly like what it is: party professionals deciding
in private which disputes the public will be allowed to see.

- @poland_event_queue: Begin comparing notes

@ko_tusk
title: Avoid the succession game and deal only with the leader
subtitle: Keep one accountable counterpart and accept that KO's neglected currents will organise around the exclusion.
on-arrival: ko_channel_target = "Formal KO leadership only"; ko_relation += 4; ko_coalition_dissent += 3; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "The Left refuses to place a bet on KO's future"

Lewica informs every KO current that formal business will go through **[+
ko_leader +]**. The public line is clean and nobody can mistake our contact for
an endorsement in a succession that has not begun. The currents left out each
conclude that influence after the current leadership will have to be built
without us.

- @poland_event_queue: Inform the currents
